  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 300 AM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nWarm, above-normal temperatures and dry conditions will continue \nfor the week ahead. The temperature spread in bias-corrected \nprobabilistic guidance is low, which indicates high confidence of \nno appreciable cool down next week. High temperatures will \ngenerally be in the 80s deg F with some locations potentially \naround 90 deg F (most likely across southwest Oklahoma into \nwestern north Texas). \n\nAn upper-level low is forecast to pass by across Texas late \nFriday into Saturday; however, the current forecast track would \nkeep any chance for rain to our southeast. Therefore, the forecast\nremains dry for now.\n\nMahale",
